  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nSurface high pressure will exit to our south and east tonight\nahead of a cold front, which will cross late tonight into early\nFriday morning. Following a dry and warm evening with mainly\nsunny skies, clouds will increase tonight with perhaps an\nisolated shower across the mtns and towards the Canadian Border.\nIt will otherwise be a mild night for late October with lows\ninto the 40s and lower 50s.\n\nPartly cloudy skies will prevail behind the front on Friday,\nalthough developing upslope flow will result in mainly cloudy\nskies across the mtns and points north. High temperatures will\nrange from the 50s across the north with 60s further to the\nsouth. West-northwest wind gusts may approach 30 mph during the\nafternoon, which will make it feel a little cooler. Friday night\nwill be cooler with CAA continuing as overnight lows fall into \nthe 20s and 30s. Cool and dry conditions are expected this \nweekend with daytime highs on Saturday into the 40s/50s before \nwarming up some on Sunday. Lows will be below freezing in most \nlocations. \n\nMainly dry conditions are likely to persist through at least the\nmiddle of next week with fluctuating temperatures, although it\nwill generally be warmer than avg.",
